    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_70ef2ac7a308101a1a10f8f80523735b9a9ff09ff939e78990c761bad51b9ca8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For primitive Selberg-class functions, the generalized explicit formula inserts the local Euler weights Lambda_F into the resonant density g_{F,alpha}; for Dirichlet characters their complex phase becomes a translation of the predicted shortage locations. Separately, the coefficient-growth exponent theta_F limits the usable Fourier and zero-sum ranges, while the degree d_F locates the pair-correlation transition and determines whether the earlier smoothing argument reaches it without an additional regularity hypothesis.",
